    "headingid": 373,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 66345,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 473,
        "headingId": 373,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Not recommended:</em> hereditary multiple cutaneous leiomyomas; multiple cutaneous and uterine leiomyomas; Reed syndrome {11549574}</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-23T16:49:56"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 461,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 374,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 66346,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 473,
        "headingId": 374,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-23T16:49:56"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 462,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 375,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 66347,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 473,
        "headingId": 375,
        "headingText": "<p>Skin, uterus, and kidney (see <a style=\"cursor:pointer\" href=\"/attachment/34/473/13464\" target=\"_blank\">#13464</a>Table&nbsp;<a style=\"cursor:pointer\" href=\"/attachment/34/473/13464\" target=\"_blank\">#13464</a>)</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-07-10T14:12:01"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 463,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 376,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 66348,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 473,
        "headingId": 376,
        "headingText": "<p>Tumours usually present with an earlier onset (see <a style=\"cursor:pointer\" href=\"/attachment/34/473/13464\" target=\"_blank\">#13464</a>Table&nbsp;<a style=\"cursor:pointer\" href=\"/attachment/34/473/13464\" target=\"_blank\">#13464</a>).</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-07-10T14:12:24"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 464,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 377,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 66349,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 473,
        "headingId": 377,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>HLRCC is rare, with uncertain prevalence; &gt;&nbsp;300&nbsp;families have been reported to date {20301430}, and 0.24% of unselected women with uterine leiomyoma are affected {30741757}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-23T16:49:56"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 465,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 378,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 66350,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 473,
        "headingId": 378,
        "headingText": "<p>HLRCC is caused by autosomal dominant inherited germline mutation of the fumarate hydratase gene (<em>FH</em>; chromosome 1q42.3-q43) {11283798; 21398687; 23211287}. More than 80 different <em>FH</em> pathogenic variants are known {15937070; 21398687}. There is no genotype&ndash;phenotype correlation {15937070}, but there is high penetrance {15724016}. Fumarate hydratase deficiency in uterine leiomyoma can also occur due to sporadic genetic alterations in the <em>FH</em> gene, unrelated to HLRCC {28664937; 26574848}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-07-07T17:31:39"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 466,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 379,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 66351,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 473,
        "headingId": 379,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The Krebs cycle enzyme fumarate hydratase converts fumarate to L-malate. Decreased fumarate hydratase activity results in fumarate accumulation, leading to tumorigenesis due to stabilization of HIF&alpha; {21398687}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-23T16:49:56"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 473,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 386,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 66352,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 473,
        "headingId": 386,
        "headingText": "<p>See <a style=\"cursor:pointer\" href=\"/attachment/34/473/13464\" target=\"_blank\">#13464</a>Table&nbsp;<a style=\"cursor:pointer\" href=\"/attachment/34/473/13464\" target=\"_blank\">#13464</a>.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-07-10T14:12:40"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 467,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 380,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 66353,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 473,
        "headingId": 380,
        "headingText": "<p>Uterine leiomyomas show a staghorn vascular pattern, alveolar pattern oedema, scattered bizarre nuclei, ovoid nuclei arranged in chains, eosinophilic cytoplasmic inclusions, and prominent eosinophilic nucleoli surrounded by perinucleolar haloes (see <a style=\"cursor:pointer\" href=\"/attachment/34/473/13464\" target=\"_blank\">#13464</a>Table&nbsp;<a style=\"cursor:pointer\" href=\"/attachment/34/473/13464\" target=\"_blank\">#13464</a>) {27454940; 26574848; 24309325}.</p>\r\n<h5><em>Immunohistochemistry</em></h5>\r\n<p>These tumours usually show loss of immunostaining for fumarate hydratase, although some cases may display retained expression due to <em>FH</em> missense mutation {31162287}. Positive immunostaining for 2SC may be more sensitive for fumarate hydratase deficiency but is currently not widely available {24441663}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-07-10T14:23:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 468,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 381,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 66354,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 473,
        "headingId": 381,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-23T16:49:56"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 469,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 382,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 66355,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 473,
        "headingId": 382,
        "headingText": "<p>The identification of <em>FH</em> germline mutation or deletion is necessary for definitive diagnosis {15937070}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-07-07T17:33:26"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 472,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 385,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 66356,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 473,
        "headingId": 385,
        "headingText": "<p>HLRCC can be suspected or confirmed if the criteria in <a style=\"cursor:pointer\" href=\"/attachment/34/473/10888\" target=\"_blank\">#10888</a>Box&nbsp;<a style=\"cursor:pointer\" href=\"/attachment/34/473/10888\" target=\"_blank\">#10888</a> are met.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-07-10T14:24:22"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 470,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 383,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 66357,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 473,
        "headingId": 383,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>RCC should be staged according to the Union for International Cancer Control (UICC) TNM classification.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-23T16:49:56"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 471,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 384,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 66358,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 473,
        "headingId": 384,
        "headingText": "<p>RCCs arising in this syndrome are aggressive {17895761; 12772087}. Although the smooth muscle tumours may show atypical cytological features, there are only rare reports of biologically malignant behaviour {27454940; 26574848; 16477632}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-07-16T15:03:38"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]